Touch: forget the finger that drives touch-to-mouse on SDL_Quit.

SDL_touch.c keeps the finger it turns into mouse events in statics that
SDL_QuitTouch did not reset. A finger held while SDL shut down never sent
its up, so after the next SDL_Init no touch made mouse events (seen on the
iPhone, build 202610231125, second test run in one launch).

diff --git a/src/events/SDL_touch.c b/src/events/SDL_touch.c
index b8ebb78..161bf11 100644
--- a/src/events/SDL_touch.c
+++ b/src/events/SDL_touch.c
@@ -612,6 +612,13 @@ void SDL_QuitTouch(void)
 
         SDL_free(SDL_touchDevices);
         SDL_touchDevices = NULL;
+
+        /* Voxelium: a finger still down when SDL quits never sends its
+         * "up", which left touch-to-mouse disabled for the next SDL_Init
+         * in the process. */
+        finger_touching = false;
+        track_touchid = 0;
+        track_fingerid = 0;
     }
     SDL_UnlockTouch();
 
